From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:15:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] WIP target/ppc: the syscall trap

Prototype, not for merge as is (no series number; needs the vendored
system/syscall-trap.c variant support in src/).

sc and scv (LEV 0) from problem state are reported from powerpc_excp()
before the per-model handlers, with NIP still at the instruction: number
r0, arguments r3-r8, pc the address after it, len 4.  ABI PPC64 when
MSR[SF] (or the BookE CM bit) is set, else PPC.  Returns are reported
from do_rfi(), which every rfi/rfid/hrfid/rfscv/rfci/rfdi/rfmci
form goes through, when the new MSR has PR set and a call is pending.

Task key: k1 is paca->kstack on Book3S-64 Linux (the PACA from SPRG1, or
HSPRG0 for a hypervisor kernel; the PACAKSAVE offset learnt from the
kernel's first "ld r1,D(r13)" after a syscall entry), SPRG3
(SPRN_SPRG_THREAD, &current->thread) otherwise; k2 is the user r1.

Return values are normalized to -errno: sc reports an error as a
positive r3 with cr0.SO set, scv as a negative r3.  CPUState gains
syscall_variant (0 sc, 1 scv), kept with each pending call.

target/ppc/sc-trap-dbg.c is a test consumer (SCTRAP_LOG=<file>), used
with tests/ppc-sctrap.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
